---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { products } from '../../data/products';

const thermostat = products.find(p => p.slug === 'ecobee-smartthermostat-premium')!;
const fan = products.find(p => p.slug === 'hunter-aerodyne-52-fan')!;
const smokeDetector = products.find(p => p.slug === 'google-nest-protect-battery')!;
const bulb = products.find(p => p.slug === 'govee-smart-bulb-rgbww')!;
const dimmer = products.find(p => p.slug === 'lutron-caseta-dimmer')!;
---

<Layout
  title="Best Smart Home Devices for Winter (2026)"
  description="The 5 best smart home devices to install before winter: a smart thermostat, ceiling fan with winter mode, CO detector, warm smart bulbs, and smart dimmer switches."
>
  <div class="bg-amber-50 border-b border-amber-100">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-2 text-xs text-amber-800 text-center">
      This site earns commissions from purchases made through our links at no extra cost to you.
    </div>
  </div>

  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">

    <nav class="text-xs text-gray-400 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-green-700">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">›</span>
      <a href="/smart-home" class="hover:text-green-700">Smart Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2">›</span>
      Best Smart Home Devices for Winter
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3 leading-tight">
      Best Smart Home Devices for Winter (2026)
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mb-8">Last updated: June 2026 · 5 winter-focused upgrades</p>

    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4 leading-relaxed">
      Winter changes what you need from your smart home. You're running heat instead of A/C, using more lighting as days shorten, relying on space heaters that pose carbon monoxide risks, and spending more time inside where comfort automation matters most. The five devices here each address a specific winter problem — energy cost, comfort, safety, and ambiance.
    </p>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-8 leading-relaxed">
      None of these require a hub, subscription, or contractor. All install in under an hour. Together they meaningfully reduce heating bills and improve the quality of your time indoors between November and March.
    </p>

    <!-- Winter Tip Banner -->
    <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-2xl p-5 mb-12">
      <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-2 text-sm">The winter smart home checklist</p>
      <ul class="space-y-1.5 text-sm text-gray-700">
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-blue-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span>Schedule your thermostat to drop 7–10°F when you sleep or leave — saves up to 10% on heating</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-blue-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span>Run ceiling fans clockwise at low speed to push warm air down from vaulted ceilings</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-blue-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span>Replace CO detector batteries before you start running the furnace for the season</li>
        <li class="flex gap-2"><span class="text-blue-500 flex-shrink-0">✓</span>Switch smart bulbs to warm white (2700–3000K) for cozy evening ambiance</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Thermostat -->
    <section id="thermostat" class="mb-14 scroll-mt-20">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="text-2xl">🌡️</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest">#1 Winter Priority</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Smart Thermostat</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Top Pick</p>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{thermostat.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2">{thermostat.tagline}</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-green-700">${thermostat.price}</p>
          </div>
          <a href={thermostat.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="inline-block bg-green-700 text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-green-800 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap">
            Check on Amazon →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">The ecobee SmartThermostat Premium is the single highest-ROI winter smart home purchase. Its included SmartSensor detects occupancy in the room where you actually spend time — the bedroom, living room — and heats that room rather than wherever the thermostat is mounted on the wall. Most homes with central HVAC see $150–$250/year in heating and cooling savings after switching to the ecobee. For the 249 price, payback typically takes 12–18 months, then it pays you back every year after.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">For winter specifically: the ecobee's scheduling lets you program a setback of 7–10°F while you're at work and sleeping — the temperature range where ENERGY STAR says you save 10% on heating. It also monitors humidity, which is important in winter when dry air makes your home feel colder than it is.</p>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4">
        <div class="bg-green-50 rounded-xl p-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-sm">Pros</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            {thermostat.pros.slice(0, 3).map(pro => <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 flex gap-2"><span class="text-green-600 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✓</span>{pro}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-red-50 rounded-xl p-4">
          <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-3 text-sm">Cons</p>
          <ul class="space-y-1.5">
            {thermostat.cons.slice(0, 3).map(con => <li class="text-sm text-gray-700 flex gap-2"><span class="text-red-500 flex-shrink-0 mt-0.5">✗</span>{con}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-thermostat-no-c-wire" class="text-sm text-green-700 hover:underline font-medium">Read the full smart thermostat guide →</a>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Ceiling Fan -->
    <section id="ceiling-fan" class="mb-14 scroll-mt-20">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="text-2xl">🌀</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest">#2 Winter Priority</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Smart Ceiling Fan (Winter Reverse Mode)</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Top Pick</p>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{fan.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2">{fan.tagline}</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-green-700">${fan.price}</p>
          </div>
          <a href={fan.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="inline-block bg-green-700 text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-green-800 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap">
            Check on Amazon →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">Most people don't know ceiling fans have a winter mode. Set to clockwise rotation at low speed, the fan gently pulls cool air up and pushes warm air (which naturally rises to the ceiling) down into the living space. In rooms with 9+ foot ceilings, this alone can reduce your perceived temperature difference by 2–4°F — meaning you set the thermostat 2–4°F lower while feeling the same. The Hunter Aerodyne is the best value smart ceiling fan: built-in WiFi, no hub, compatible with Alexa, Google Home, and Apple HomeKit.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">The winter reverse mode is accessible via the Alexa/Google voice command ("Alexa, set the fan to reverse") or through the Hunter app. At low speed, the Aerodyne draws only 18W — negligible energy cost for meaningful heating efficiency gain.</p>
      <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-ceiling-fans" class="text-sm text-green-700 hover:underline font-medium">Read the full smart ceiling fan guide →</a>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. CO Detector -->
    <section id="co-detector" class="mb-14 scroll-mt-20">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="text-2xl">🚨</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest">#3 Winter Priority</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Smart CO + Smoke Detector</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Top Pick</p>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{smokeDetector.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2">{smokeDetector.tagline}</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-green-700">${smokeDetector.price}</p>
          </div>
          <a href={smokeDetector.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="inline-block bg-green-700 text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-green-800 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap">
            Check on Amazon →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">Carbon monoxide exposure peaks in winter. Furnaces, water heaters, fireplaces, and gas ranges all produce CO — and when they're sealed up tight against the cold, a malfunctioning appliance can raise indoor CO to dangerous levels faster than in summer. The Google Nest Protect speaks your location and the hazard type out loud rather than just beeping, so you know which room and what type of danger before you're even fully awake.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">The Nest Protect app sends notifications to your phone if CO or smoke is detected while you're away — critical for catching a furnace malfunction before you come home to a dangerous situation. It self-tests 400 times per day and alerts you when battery is low, so you're never caught with a dead detector.</p>
      <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-smoke-detector" class="text-sm text-green-700 hover:underline font-medium">Read the full smart smoke detector guide →</a>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Smart Bulbs -->
    <section id="smart-bulbs" class="mb-14 scroll-mt-20">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="text-2xl">💡</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest">#4 Winter Priority</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Warm White Smart Bulbs</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Top Pick</p>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{bulb.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2">{bulb.tagline}</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-green-700">${bulb.price}/bulb</p>
          </div>
          <a href={bulb.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="inline-block bg-green-700 text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-green-800 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap">
            Check on Amazon →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">Winter evenings are long and lighting sets the tone for your entire indoor experience. Smart RGBWW bulbs let you shift to warm amber light (2200–2700K) in the evening — the color temperature that matches candlelight and firelight, proven to reduce cortisol and help with sleep onset. The Govee RGBWW at $12/bulb is the most affordable color + tunable white bulb available, with no hub required. Set a sunset automation that shifts your living room from cool daylight white to warm amber at 5pm.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">For homeowners wanting more reliability and ecosystem depth, the Philips Hue White Ambiance or Color bulbs are worth the premium — better app, faster response, and rock-solid Zigbee protocol. But for most people, Govee at $12/bulb is hard to argue with.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. Smart Dimmer -->
    <section id="smart-dimmer" class="mb-14 scroll-mt-20">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
        <span class="text-2xl">🎛️</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest">#5 Winter Priority</p>
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">Smart Dimmer Switch</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 mb-4">
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start justify-between gap-4">
          <div>
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold text-green-700 uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Top Pick</p>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">{dimmer.name}</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm mb-2">{dimmer.tagline}</p>
            <p class="text-xl font-bold text-green-700">${dimmer.price}/switch</p>
          </div>
          <a href={dimmer.affiliateUrl} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener" class="inline-block bg-green-700 text-white px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg font-semibold text-sm hover:bg-green-800 transition-colors whitespace-nowrap">
            Check on Amazon →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-3">A smart dimmer lets you set evening scenes — dim to 30% in the living room at 7pm, use full brightness in the kitchen, and have the bedroom automatically drop to 10% at 9pm — all triggered by time or voice without touching a switch. The Lutron Caseta is the gold standard for a reason: it doesn't use your home Wi-Fi (uses Lutron's dedicated RF protocol), so it never drops connection, never lags, and works even when your router restarts.</p>
      <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-light-switches" class="text-sm text-green-700 hover:underline font-medium">Read the full smart switch guide →</a>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Guides -->
    <section class="border-t border-gray-100 pt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-thermostat-no-c-wire" class="group block border border-gray-100 rounded-xl p-4 hover:border-green-200 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
          <p class="text-xs text-green-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Smart Home</p>
          <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 text-sm group-hover:text-green-700 transition-colors">Best Smart Thermostat (No C-Wire) →</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-smoke-detector" class="group block border border-gray-100 rounded-xl p-4 hover:border-green-200 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
          <p class="text-xs text-green-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Smart Home</p>
          <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 text-sm group-hover:text-green-700 transition-colors">Best Smart Smoke Detectors →</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/backup-power/best-generator-for-ice-storms" class="group block border border-gray-100 rounded-xl p-4 hover:border-green-200 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
          <p class="text-xs text-green-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Backup Power</p>
          <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 text-sm group-hover:text-green-700 transition-colors">Best Generator for Ice Storms →</p>
        </a>
        <a href="/smart-home/best-smart-ceiling-fans" class="group block border border-gray-100 rounded-xl p-4 hover:border-green-200 hover:shadow-sm transition-all">
          <p class="text-xs text-green-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest mb-1">Smart Home</p>
          <p class="font-medium text-gray-900 text-sm group-hover:text-green-700 transition-colors">Best Smart Ceiling Fans →</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>
</Layout>
